        "---\n",
        "title: \"Advanced Decision Trees\"\n",
        "subtitle: \"Bagging, Random Forests, and Boosting in Market Data\"\n",
        "author: \"Miguel Fonseca\"\n",
        "format:\n",
        "  revealjs:\n",
        "    toc: true\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "# Motivation \n",
        "\n",
        "## Motivation: Why Ensembles in Finance? {.scrollable}\n",
        "\n",
        "- Financial data are:\n",
        "  - Noisy\n",
        "  - Non-stationary\n",
        "  - High-dimensional\n",
        "- Single models:\n",
        "  - Overfit easily\n",
        "  - Are unstable to small data changes\n",
        "\n",
        "**Ensembles = robustness + better generalization**\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Typical Financial Use Cases {.scrollable}\n",
        "\n",
        "- Equity return prediction (regression)\n",
        "- Market direction (up/down) classification\n",
        "- Volatility forecasting\n",
        "- Credit risk & default prediction\n",
        "- Fraud detection\n",
        "- Portfolio signal aggregation\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Bias–Variance Tradeoff (Finance Perspective) {.scrollable}\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\mathbb{E}[(Y - \\hat{f}(X))^2]\n",
        "=\n",
        "\\text{Bias}^2 + \\text{Variance} + \\text{Noise}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "- Markets have **high noise**\n",
        "- Variance reduction is often more valuable than bias reduction\n",
        "\n",
        "| Model | Bias | Variance |\n",
        "|------|------|----------|\n",
        "| Single tree | Low | High |\n",
        "| Bagging | Same | ↓ |\n",
        "| Random Forest | Same | ↓↓ |\n",
        "| Boosting | ↓ | ↑ (controlled) |\n",
        "\n",
        "# Bagging\n",
        "\n",
        "## Core idea {.scrollable}\n",
        "\n",
        "> Train many trees on resampled data and average predictions\n",
        "\n",
        "**Algorithm:**\n",
        "\n",
        "1. Draw $B$ bootstrap samples\n",
        "2. Train a tree on each sample\n",
        "3. Aggregate predictions\n",
        "\n",
        "**Finance intuition:**\n",
        "\n",
        "- Reduces sensitivity to **outliers**\n",
        "- Stabilizes signals from noisy indicators\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Bagging for Financial Returns {.scrollable}\n",
        "\n",
        "### Example \n",
        "\n",
        "- Target: next-day return\n",
        "- Features:\n",
        "  - Lagged returns\n",
        "  - Moving averages\n",
        "  - Volatility measures\n",
        "  - Volume indicators\n",
        "\n",
        "**Why bagging helps:**\n",
        "\n",
        "- One bad split $\\neq$ one bad model\n",
        "- Averaging smooths extreme forecasts\n",
        "\n",
        "# Random Forests\n",
        "\n",
        "## Key idea {.scrollable}\n",
        "\n",
        "> Bagging + feature randomness\n",
        "\n",
        "**At each split:**\n",
        "\n",
        "- Only a random subset of features is considered\n",
        "\n",
        "**Effect:**\n",
        "\n",
        "- Trees become **less correlated**\n",
        "- Variance decreases further\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Random Forest Algorithm {.scrollable}\n",
        "\n",
        "For $b = 1,...,B$:\n",
        "\n",
        "  1. Bootstrap the data\n",
        "  2. Grow a deep tree\n",
        "     - At each split, sample m features\n",
        "     - Choose best split among them\n",
        "Aggregate predictions\n",
        "\n",
        "Typical defaults:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Classification: $m = \\sqrt{p}$\n",
        "- Regression: $m = \\frac{p}{3}$\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Random Forests in Finance {.scrollable}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        ":::{.columns}\n",
        "::::{.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "### Strengths\n",
        "\n",
        "Excellent baseline for:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Cross-sectional stock selection\n",
        "- Credit scoring\n",
        "- Fraud detection\n",
        "\n",
        "Handles:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Non-linearities\n",
        "- Interactions\n",
        "- Mixed feature types\n",
        "::::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::{.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "### Limitations\n",
        "\n",
        "- Poor extrapolation\n",
        "- Weak for regime shifts\n",
        "- Limited interpretability\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Out-of-Bag (OOB) Error {.scrollable}\n",
        "\n",
        "- ~36% of observations are excluded from each bootstrap sample\n",
        "- Can be used as a validation set\n",
        "\n",
        "Useful when:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Time-series CV is expensive\n",
        "- Dataset is small\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.callout-warning title=\"In finance:\"}\n",
        "- Still respect time ordering\n",
        "- OOB $\\neq$ time-aware validation\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Out-of-Bag (OOB) Error\n",
        "\n",
        "- Each tree in a  \n",
        "  **Random Forest**  \n",
        "  is trained on a **bootstrap sample**\n",
        "- ~63.2% of observations are used\n",
        "- ~36.8% are **Out-of-Bag (OOB)**\n",
        "\n",
        "For each observation:\n",
        "\n",
        "- Collect predictions **only from trees that did NOT see it**\n",
        "- Aggregate (vote / mean)\n",
        "- Compare with true value\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Why 36.8%?\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\begin{align*}\n",
        "P(\\text{not selected}) =\n",
        "\\left(1 - \\frac{1}{n}\\right)^n\n",
        "\\approx e^{-1} \\approx 0.368\n",
        "\\end{align*}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "### OOB Error\n",
        "\n",
        "- Classification → Misclassification rate  \n",
        "- Regression → MSE  \n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\text{OOB Error} =\n",
        "\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{i=1}^n\n",
        "L(y_i, \\widehat{y}_i^{OOB})\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## OOB Error in Python {.scrollable}"
      ],
      "id": "4a0c9063"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.ensemble import RandomForestClassifier\n",
        "from sklearn.datasets import make_classification\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "\n",
        "X, y = make_classification(n_samples=1000, n_features=20, random_state=42)\n",
        "\n",
        "rf = RandomForestClassifier(\n",
        "    n_estimators=200,\n",
        "    oob_score=True,\n",
        "    bootstrap=True,\n",
        "    random_state=42\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "rf.fit(X, y)\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"OOB Score:\", rf.oob_score_)\n",
        "print(\"OOB Error:\", 1 - rf.oob_score_)"
      ],
